Reached by: the Sound widget (click, scroll, middle-click), the XF86Audio keys, and System → Sound.
Symptom: VGS has no volume control, device picker, per-app mixer or volume OSD.

## Scope
- Kinds `service`, `bar-widget`, `panel`, `pane`. Capabilities `status`, `surfaces`, `ipc`, `configure`, `shortcut`, `layers`, `screens`, `requirements`.
- `Quickshell.Services.Pipewire` in-process. Lists come from timer-refreshed snapshots, never Repeaters on the live model (Omarchy `audio/Panel.qml:102-107` records a Quickshell PipeWire crash). The input meter is `PwNodePeakMonitor`, enabled only while shown.
- Default device:
  - set `preferredDefaultAudioSink`/`Source`;
  - move already-playing application streams with optional `pactl move-sink-input`;
  - move only streams with `application.name`, skipping EasyEffects and filter-chain outputs (Omarchy `bin/omarchy-audio-output-set-default`);
  - without `pactl`, offer it and state that playing streams stay.
- The volume target resolves through a DSP/filter default sink to the physical sink (Omarchy `audio/Panel.qml:111-131`).
- Keys `volume-up`/`down`/`mute`/`mic-mute` on XF86Audio* (Q3, with the `foreignBinds` choice from S04); `LevelOsd` on the focused screen; `volumeStep` (unit `%`, presets 2/5/10).
- README with a shot.

## Acceptance
- `scripts/test-sound-logic.js`: level glyph, step clamp, stream move filter, DSP resolution; with controls.
- New row `scripts/smoke/rows/sound.sh` on the sandbox PipeWire (S08):
  - the widget follows a volume set in the pane;
  - choosing the second null sink makes it default and moves an already-playing test stream (control: no move);
  - with the filter-chain sink as default, the slider moves the physical null sink (control: it moves the filter sink);
  - a key raises by the step and shows the OSD;
  - PipeWire stopped gives the unavailable state;
  - keyboard-only path.
  - Control: a widget that starts a process.

