Reached by: the VPN widget and System → VPN.
Symptom: VGS cannot show Tailscale state, connect, choose an exit node, switch accounts or log in.

## Scope
- Kinds `service`, `bar-widget`, `panel`, `pane`. Capabilities `status`, `surfaces`, `ipc`, `configure`, `system`, `requirements`, `run`.
- Poll of `tailscale status --json`:
  - every 30 s while idle (unit `s`, presets 10/30/60), every 3 s while open;
  - one poll in flight;
  - a 10 s watchdog that a refresh cannot postpone;
  - bounded `data` status.
- Exit nodes: each peer has a UI id and a separate CLI target (DNSName, else HostName, else the first IPv4; Mullvad uses its IPv4). `set --exit-node=<target>`; never a raw peer id (Omarchy `Service.qml:128-134,327-344`).
- Commands `up`, `down`, `switch`, `exit-node list`. Login opens the parsed auth URL through `run.detached(['xdg-open', url])`.
- Setup: requirement `tailscale` → Install; `service-tailscaled` and `tailscale-operator` steps → Enable, Allow.
- README with a shot.

## Acceptance
- `scripts/test-vpn-logic.js` on recorded `status --json`: running, stopped, logged out, Mullvad, access denied; the exit-node target rule. Control: a target equal to the peer id.
- New row `scripts/smoke/rows/vpn.sh` with stand-in `tailscale` and `xdg-open`:
  - toggling runs `up`/`down`;
  - exit node runs `set --exit-node=<dns name>`;
  - access denied offers Allow;
  - a hung stand-in poll is killed at 10 s while refreshes continue;
  - the poll interval follows open and closed;
  - login records the URL and opens no browser;
  - keyboard-only path.
  - Control: a widget that polls on its own.

## References
- docs/plans/v2-system-plan.md §3.4
- tmp/omarchy-ref/shell/plugins/panels/tailscale/Service.qml:45,128-185,293-362,389-445

Reached by: every brightness control in S16 and S17.
Symptom: VGS v2 cannot read or set brightness on any display. v1 drove the Pro Display XDR and Studio Display over HID, external monitors over DDC, and internal panels through the backlight.

The offline tests can start at once. The fake HID server comes from S08.

## Scope
- `helper/brightness.py` (python3, one-shot, JSON): `list` and `set <id> <percent>`.
- Apple:
  - vendor 05ac; 9243 raw 400–50000; 1114 raw 400–60000;
  - hidraw interfaces grouped by their USB parent device (sysfs devpath) plus serial;
  - probe with a zeroed report id 1 via HIDIOCGFEATURE(7) = _IOC(R|W,'H',0x07,7), accept only in-range answers (ceiling 60000), prefer usage page 0x82 / usage 0x0001;
  - write HIDIOCSFEATURE(7) = _IOC(R|W,'H',0x06,7), bytes 1..4 little-endian;
  - linear clamped mapping;
  - a kernel backlight on the device is preferred;
  - no asdcontrol.
- DDC: `ddcutil detect` cached 30 s and invalidated on hotplug; `getvcp 10 --brief` and `setvcp 10`.
- Backlight: `brightnessctl`.
- Mapping: serial to EDID serial; else a unique model; else unassigned.
- Access reported as separate states: hidraw RW; ddcutil missing; i2c module not loaded; nodes inaccessible.
- Test seams `VGS_SYSFS_ROOT`, `VGS_DEV_ROOT`, `VGS_HID_FAKE`.
- Write the decision record "one-shot plugin helper over hidraw, DDC and backlight; uaccess-only rule" (the D010 justification), with the measured startup-plus-write figure, naming tool and run. Write docs/architecture/displays.md.

## Acceptance
- `scripts/test-displays-brightness.py`:
  - bytes for 0/50/100 % on both models (XDR 100 % = 50000);
  - ioctl numbers;
  - rejection above the ceiling;
  - descriptor preference;
  - two same-product units with no or equal serials stay distinct by USB parent;
  - DDC and backlight parsing;
  - the access states;
  - the seam asserts no real device opens.
  - Controls: a big-endian encoder, a wrong ioctl, product+serial grouping, a hardcoded interface.

